---
import { docsHref } from "../lib/site";

const workflows = [
  { title: "Know who needs you.", text: "Working, idle, or waiting for your answer. Agent state lives beside the pane, so the next decision is a jump away—not a tour of every tab.", detail: "phux agent list", href: "/agents", link: "Connect your agents" },
  { title: "Leave the window. Keep the work.", text: "Shells and agents run on a background server. Detach the TUI, quit the desktop, then return to the same running session.", detail: "phux attach work", href: "/concepts#what-survives-what", link: "See what stays running" },
  { title: "Put your other machines to work.", text: "Add a host over SSH, then attach directly over QUIC. Find your Tailscale machines from the desktop. No phux account or hosted control plane.", detail: "phux host add me@mini", href: "/remote", link: "Connect a machine" },
  { title: "Review the work. Send it back.", text: "On macOS/Linux, read local diffs, stage selected lines, and commit beside your terminals. Add line notes for the agent. Open GitHub pull requests in the desktop’s Reviews view.", detail: "Changes + Reviews · Desktop", href: "/desktop-changes", link: "See the review workflow" },
  { title: "Make a project repeatable.", text: "Keep tabs, panes, and startup commands in a checked-in recipe. Open each checkout in its own session, and group related work across machines.", detail: "phux project open", href: "/projects", link: "Set up your project" },
  { title: "Let agents drive, too.", text: "Agents can read a pane, run a command, wait for a result, and hand work to another agent. Use the CLI, MCP, or an integration—not a second hidden workspace.", detail: "phux mcp", href: "/agent-quickstart", link: "Give your agent the controls" },
];
---
<section class="workflow-proof" aria-labelledby="workflow-title">
  <div class="agent-fit">
    <p>Bring your agents. Keep your editor.</p>
    <p class="agent-names">Claude Code <span>·</span> Codex <span>·</span> OpenCode <span>·</span> pi <span>·</span> Oh My Pi <span>·</span> Grok</p>
    <a href={docsHref("/agents#agent-setup")}>Integrations, MCP, and any CLI agent <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
  </div>
  <header><p class="eyebrow">From first prompt to reviewed code</p><h2 id="workflow-title">More work in flight.<br />Less work keeping track.</h2></header>
  <div class="workflow-grid">
    {workflows.map((workflow, index) => (
      <article>
        <span class="step" aria-hidden="true">0{index + 1}</span>
        <h3>{workflow.title}</h3>
        <p>{workflow.text}</p>
        <code>{workflow.detail}</code>
        <a href={docsHref(workflow.href)}>{workflow.link} <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      </article>
    ))}
  </div>
  <p class="boundary">Work stays running while the server does. A server crash or machine reboot ends running programs. Agent integrations report lifecycle events; other agents can use terminal-based detection.</p>
</section>

<section class="control-proof" aria-labelledby="control-title">
  <div>
    <p class="eyebrow">Human at the controls. Agents on the tools.</p>
    <h2 id="control-title">Stop polling tabs.<br />Wait for what matters.</h2>
    <p>See the same terminals your agents can read and operate. Inspect the current state, wait for an agent to need you, then send a follow-up to its exact pane.</p>
    <a href={docsHref("/agents#driving-an-agent-in-a-pane")}>The agent control loop <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
  </div>
  <figure>
    <figcaption>Real commands · an example workflow, not a live feed</figcaption>
    <pre><code><span># See who is doing what</span>{"\n"}phux agent list{"\n\n"}<span># Wait for the next agent that needs you</span>{"\n"}phux agent wait --any --until blocked --timeout 600{"\n\n"}<span># Inspect its pane before sending input</span>{"\n"}phux snapshot @7{"\n\n"}<span># Send a follow-up to that exact agent</span>{"\n"}phux agent prompt @7 'Run the tests again'</code></pre>
    <p>Use the pane returned by your own agent list. A wait observes a new transition; a delivery receipt is not proof the work is finished.</p>
  </figure>
</section>

<section class="product-fit" aria-labelledby="fit-title">
  <div>
    <p class="eyebrow">Choosing your workspace</p>
    <h2 id="fit-title">Your terminal is the workspace.<br />The window is your choice.</h2>
    <p>Use a native desktop, stay in your terminal, or build on the same server with code. phux is for people who want agent-aware terminals without moving their whole workflow into another editor.</p>
  </div>
  <aside>
    <h3>Considering Orca?</h3>
    <p>Orca brings an editor, browser, worktrees, and task integrations together. phux puts the shared terminal server, native clients, and agent controls at the center. Both offer automation and remote sessions.</p>
    <a href={docsHref("/compare#phux-vs-orca")}>Compare the workflows, category by category <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    <p class="fit-note">Sources and trade-offs for agents, review, remote work, automation, and platform support.</p>
  </aside>
</section>

<style>
  section { margin-top: 72px; border-top: 1px solid var(--color-rule); padding-top: 48px; }
  h2 { margin: 0; color: var(--color-fg); font-size: clamp(30px, 3.5vw, 44px); line-height: 1.12; font-weight: 500; letter-spacing: -.045em; }
  h3 { margin: 0; color: var(--color-fg); font-size: 23px; font-weight: 500; line-height: 1.2; letter-spacing: -.035em; }
  p { color: var(--color-muted); font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.7; }
  a { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 12px; min-height: 44px; color: var(--color-fg); font-size: 13px; }
  a:hover { text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 4px; }
  a:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--color-accent); outline-offset: 4px; }
  .eyebrow { margin: 0 0 16px; color: var(--color-dim); font-size: 12px; }
  .agent-fit { margin-bottom: 64px; text-align: center; }
  .agent-fit > p:first-child { margin: 0 0 12px; }
  .agent-names { margin: 0; color: var(--color-fg); font-size: clamp(15px, 1.6vw, 19px); line-height: 1.8; }
  .agent-names span { padding-inline: 8px; color: var(--color-dim); }
  .agent-fit a { color: var(--color-muted); font-size: 12px; }
  .workflow-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 48px 40px; margin-top: 40px; }
  article { display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: start; min-width: 0; }
  .step { margin-bottom: 16px; color: var(--color-dim); font: 12px var(--font-code); }
  article p { margin: 14px 0 18px; }
  article code { margin-top: auto; color: var(--color-fg); font-size: 12px; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
  article a { color: var(--color-muted); }
  .boundary { margin: 24px 0 0; max-width: 100ch; color: var(--color-dim); font-size: 12px; }
  .control-proof, .product-fit { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1.1fr; gap: 64px; align-items: center; }
  .control-proof > div > p:not(.eyebrow), .product-fit > div > p:not(.eyebrow) { max-width: 48ch; margin: 20px 0 12px; }
  figure { min-width: 0; margin: 0; padding: 24px; background: var(--color-surface); border: 1px solid var(--color-rule); border-radius: 10px; }
  figcaption, figure p { color: var(--color-muted); font-size: 12px; line-height: 1.7; }
  pre { margin: 24px 0; overflow-x: auto; font-size: 12px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--color-fg); }
  pre span { color: var(--color-muted); }
  figure p { margin: 0; }
  aside { padding-left: 32px; border-left: 1px solid var(--color-rule); }
  aside p { margin: 16px 0 8px; }
  aside .fit-note { color: var(--color-dim); font-size: 12px; }
  @media (max-width: 900px) { .workflow-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 36px 28px; } .control-proof, .product-fit { gap: 28px; } }
  @media (max-width: 650px) {
    section { margin-top: 48px; padding-top: 32px; }
    .agent-fit { text-align: left; margin-bottom: 40px; }
    .agent-names span { padding-inline: 3px; }
    .workflow-grid, .control-proof, .product-fit { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .workflow-grid { gap: 28px; margin-top: 32px; }
    article { padding-bottom: 20px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-rule); }
    article h3 { font-size: 25px; }
    .step { margin-bottom: 10px; }
    article p { margin-block: 12px; }
    figure { padding: 20px; }
    aside { padding: 24px 0 0; border-left: 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--color-rule); }
  }
</style>
